respectively. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The general solution of the system is\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix} = c_{1}e^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (3t) \\\\ \\sin (3t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}e^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (3t) \\\\ \\cos (3t)\\end{bmatrix}, c_{1}, c_{2} ∈ R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when $c_{1} = 1$ and $c_{2} = 0$, we obtain the following curve:\n$e^{2t}\\sin (3t)$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548524} {:answer/id #uuid "d93ff637-1a41-5c2a-a409-3b1e7bff5ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548778} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d1f152-2d71-5a47-a7da-fd041217b7f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd46fd9-4ec6-5d4d-b935-c34269ce5266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548524} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5178042-2ee2-5608-860d-fde87cfb2607" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164433} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa9f4f97-14d1-55b4-9c75-c0369f27d217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164438} {:answer/id #uuid "78ed1003-d99d-5872-97f8-588ec6238b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78ed1003-d99d-5872-97f8-588ec6238b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164439} :answer-field/id #uuid "229c4e17-18f4-5a25-a3a7-ad03a2c43219" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164437} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d77f20-50bb-5041-953a-ea082d349ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164441} {:answer/id #uuid "60a77c64-e842-5662-bb2f-cbdc11bd2d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d77f20-50bb-5041-953a-ea082d349ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164441} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5854489-3f0b-5548-88e3-77733556dd5c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164440} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31e8870d-1899-5a7c-b624-2ee90b8a36c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164444} {:answer/id #uuid "433374ef-1e20-5498-9385-d85aff501e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "433374ef-1e20-5498-9385-d85aff501e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164445} :answer-field/id #uuid "263fab48-20ed-5d24-9308-1c953e7d4b25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186164443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0d2fdbc8-ed30-59a9-869b-569e3f094dfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-332947" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9aa8e2fec9812145eba6ef3add63dfcf16c9ddeb5557c3d37ef511947ace2e52.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i},$ where $a,b\\in R,$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that the given curve is $\\text{bounded}$ (and closed), representing $\\text{an ellipse}$ (circle) that is traversed $\\text{clockwise}.$\n\nBut we have that:\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a>0,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a<0.$\n\nThus, we must have $a=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167230 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d09c368-867e-5295-888f-2d5522e93320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305264} {:answer/id #uuid "5beb30d1-23c2-5075-8b1d-e091046c0f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306034} {:answer/id #uuid "756d2617-b102-56a0-a522-8dec631437dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d09c368-867e-5295-888f-2d5522e93320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305264} :answer-field/id #uuid "d914bbc6-a082-50f7-9cda-a921caccdc7a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d876dd6-796c-5def-b786-b647e283b215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305427} {:answer/id #uuid "63a2a224-f9e6-5b06-a51f-fab909a03aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306117} {:answer/id #uuid "9288b3fd-6217-5dc0-a6cc-d0617247a0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306540} {:answer/id #uuid "a37e88b2-535b-56bf-a159-1c96e37285da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306691} {:answer/id #uuid "b15a28f9-090d-55da-8b02-5c72519ebdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306817} {:answer/id #uuid "c00d3090-adac-5dc6-9f55-3e991a3b631d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63a2a224-f9e6-5b06-a51f-fab909a03aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306117} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2c442a-e93e-5d94-8ad6-003d643e840d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "09a5051d-6218-52fc-9de8-8eb98b5a1f5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-332952" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=9x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =1\\pm 6\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=1>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78cd39aa-7c90-5687-8921-043f0fa60b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306301} {:answer/id #uuid "c000e321-1f93-5d5b-8be0-0582d02d5083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c000e321-1f93-5d5b-8be0-0582d02d5083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306942} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e0c5c9c-4b15-55f5-af61-95dd51b0b571" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307573} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75921d4a-63e5-5aa7-9cd5-c509cdb8734a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306269} {:answer/id #uuid "75d63806-2706-519b-b12d-0ea52acabb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75921d4a-63e5-5aa7-9cd5-c509