f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7cadb25-011c-5ce5-9daf-8e2c73548bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306867} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1cc31f2-55a8-51f8-a762-087d512fc575" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd7f6a8a-46ea-55af-8487-3a48b0b2a59e" :question/math-academy-id "q-334307" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =-2\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=-2<0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable spiral (sink)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308498 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1f7d2b-7737-5d6f-b1d3-38ade4b48d36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305275} {:answer/id #uuid "7e53c5be-789c-53ec-ab7b-33e604c99edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306359} {:answer/id #uuid "f9496859-5c78-5511-a473-7ba037c12c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "phase portrait" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9496859-5c78-5511-a473-7ba037c12c71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "phase portrait" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307460} :answer-field/id #uuid "281925e0-c622-5b12-be72-f47b528ccb78" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5afa1989-0b81-51e3-a09c-e1924d66e52e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "phase portrait" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306023} {:answer/id #uuid "f183aac4-afd0-5b24-b588-862e13e81693" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "vector field" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5afa1989-0b81-51e3-a09c-e1924d66e52e" :answer/type {: