}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={{field-1}} \\\\ y &={{field-2}}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{20}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.52$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.52$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/18/18f4793f4f1edc907e28b0e148510dd3c8131a544fb703d91d0a1feb0cd8a4d1.png)\n\nAs $t\\to \\infty ,$ the curve\n{{field-5}}.\nSo, we have\n{{field-6}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-7}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-8}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe {{field-9}} of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/c0/c001f8a99c09e3d1da8c6107a298989c03e64ec58c23319ce0837a757c5ddafd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={e}^{-2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ y &={e}^{-2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{20}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.52$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.52$ | $0.53$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/2b/2b273edc4f977f2bee4d9a8c41128d4f2071ec39b0840610cbb7ee44492aae3e.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)|\\le 1,$ $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)|\\le 1,$ and ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, the curve $\\text{converges}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we have $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nAgain, since ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/c0/c001f8a99c09e3d1da8c6107a298989c03e64ec58c23319ce0837a757c5ddafd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1965cc4-138a-59cb-b873-02c363d95405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307091} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d1635c-7655-57fd-8bb9-9bec52814f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9d1635c-7655-57fd-8bb9-9bec52814f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307306} :answer-field/id #uuid "05c1b14a-0e24-5eef-b8ce-dad624ac68c0" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307542} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "342a3cb7-ff50-58ef-8f5c-9bf641ce5b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305646} {:answer/id #uuid "449fe7aa-267a-5427-acc3-1d5d024ecf43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "449fe7aa-267a-5427-acc3-1d5d024ecf43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a<0