da =a\\pm b\\text{i}$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-5}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\nHence, \n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to 0,$ we require $a<0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fefd856-04bf-577c-84fb-f1491b46729e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305463} {:answer/id #uuid "23bc3010-a290-511b-b88f-337cc7543eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305492} {:answer/id #uuid "5673d8b2-a06e-59ce-839f-2146f2a4dbb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305987} {:answer/id #uuid "6274a4d7-2544-5637-8de6-7c9b9697da44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6274a4d7-2544-5637-8de6-7c9b9697da44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306105} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a27e258-bef9-5965-b466-00a4ea9ae346" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ed50fc1-017a-52d9-9ff4-cae2ef8a72ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305598} {:answer/id #uuid "36d76e70-b9f3-50a6-80b2-b0ae37c78ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305681} {:answer/id #uuid "798a1cf7-4c45-5a13-8036-c309fd9b54c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306307} {:answer/id #uuid "8d49694c-1ded-5171-9fd9-3a2bfa2b8103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306489} {:answer/id #uuid "d87274c0-1b77-5c4b-8c5f-4ed3ece1e892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307157} {:answer/id #uuid "f7383641-560b-58d9-b5e6-21ef81d10e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ed50fc1-017a-52d9-9ff4-cae2ef8a72ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305598} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77dd0bf-aa34-5abd-bd76-903f05843194" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308100}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "25dc255f-1285-5a57-9fc0-d28154b2f004" :question/math-academy-id "q-334304" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)-7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t)+4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =4\\pm 7\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=4>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f9bd99-e77f-5e4e-9db3-8bb568f9310d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305482} {:answer/id #uuid "33b33222-0be5-5522-abfe-f437c5237327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305637} {:answer/id #uuid "5e60a010-0bd4-5b23-9d7b-cd51ae1be986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306057} {:answer/id #uuid "650b8413-f499-5752-85f7-b2a0d94c4357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306125} {:answer/id #uuid "8d664ead-6d7e-5ccd-acb2-a7d2cc6b3048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306492} {:answer/id #uuid "fc6dc8e9-bf03-5647-983f-3a5d37785edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d664ead-6d7e-5ccd-acb2-a7d2cc6b3048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306492} :answer-field/id #uuid "016a07c4-4294-5c5e-8477-eab54506e764" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307521} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0beecb-228d-5714-93e3-1b64c8b338da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306343} {:answer/id #uuid "815fba2e-56de-5c0f-9ae1-90d44760483d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306387} {:answer/id #uuid "a795ffa4-8fd3-5e6b-b566-4a944ef62e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "815fba2e-56de-5c0f-9ae1-90d44760483d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306387} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2040d15-1d78-5c0a-a9aa-e3fb10af8ee4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2847a1e4-c6b3-5129-a8ea-a4d0cc32fc5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334313" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=-1<0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable spiral (sink)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308595 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a10e698-91d2-5c37-afd2-46c5e2d14d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306470} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4b1c92-2e4b-5864-843c-a7b3e4b2381d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307203} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f78807-05a3-57a4-ab92-a617259081be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a10e698-91d2-5c37-afd2-46c5e2d14d4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306470} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d13ab71-f658-5b04-bb32