 #uuid "5135b71f-be3d-52ef-8147-88cc2add6395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "clockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385203} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca3c306-de5b-552d-903d-c143eee6bc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ca3c306-de5b-552d-903d-c143eee6bc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385204} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4740f02-fd28-5810-b644-0dde3e3c07e6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f5d02c9-9292-553c-8b42-111175736740" :question/math-academy-id "q-334291" :question/problem "![](images/95/95ad67abf7291e83476f26216aac2b48a91adf3da102ca73ffab2a29c9716514.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i}$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-5}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\nHence, \n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow notice that the given curve is $\\text{unbounded},$ representing $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$ Thus, we must have $a\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, notice that the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{infinity}.$\n\nHence, to insure that ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty ,$ we require $a>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391460 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9e6f595-8087-5dbd-8139-304da120ec34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391462} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4b344f-3032-50e7-811d-0221005ce729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd4b344f-3032-50e7-811d-0221005ce729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391463} :answer-field/id #uuid "aafde8dd-f176-57c0-adc4-2c7ebf5d023e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391461} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232eea7c-31f4-5544-b643-147187a62d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391465} {:answer/id #uuid "a193c202-a97b-5b41-872a-fce67dcd5ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/