592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "counterclockwise" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391473} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f3b7e68-3862-5d55-b31c-8ef864ba966e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ade9d10e-8ab5-5b95-969f-539a44434240" :question/math-academy-id "q-334273" :question/problem "![](images/28/2856c3b26abc3df90c228f4df3b95d9ee04a5c6cfd83cee78d1f6601c4bf8bdd.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two complex eigenvalues $\\lambda =a\\pm b\\text{i},$ where $a,b\\in R,$ is shown above. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe given curve is \n{{field-1}},\nrepresenting\n{{field-2}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-3}}.\nThus, we must have \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that the given curve is $\\text{bounded}$ (and closed), representing $\\text{an ellipse}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nBut we have that:\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a>0,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{at}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty $ when $a<0.$\n\nThus, we must have $a=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ae65751-95a4-59cf-8378-ff6dcd4e1cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a spiral" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427032} {:answer/id #uuid "9187d439-6066-5341-b833-bfb001eced5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9187d439-6066-5341-b833-bfb001eced5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ellipse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427044} :answer-field/id #uuid "67fe24b1-f8bf-5e58-ba73-46d45bbacc6e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1603c7b9-db79-5f4e-aaaa-8db20bd28197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426988} {:answer/id #uuid "c6235c16-97de-5d7d-9ce8-5b49098e30d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "unbounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1603c7b9-db79-5f4e-aaaa-8db20bd28197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "bounded" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426988} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b392be-6bfe-5887-a4ae-2c2f7f38f0c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f6c408e-5799-5dd