 we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.54$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.54$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/30/30d1e296e7c83fa8925feb116c9035de14790e89ddad37ab44710feacadf13a8.png)\n\nAs $t\\to \\infty ,$ the curve\n{{field-5}}.\nSo, we have\n{{field-6}}\nthat is traversed \n{{field-7}}.\n\nThe spiral is traversed toward \n{{field-8}}\nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe {{field-9}} of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/05/054b319170c634494c703d9588419cb6e44414196c970ca0c39689bc62f90d97.png)" :question/worked-solution "The general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}={c}_{1}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}{e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFor example, when ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we obtain the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ y &={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0.54$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $0.54$ | $0.59$ |\n\nLet's sketch this solution in the phase space.\n\n![](images/30/30d1e296e7c83fa8925feb116c9035de14790e89ddad37ab44710feacadf13a8.png)\n\nNotice that $|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)|\\le 1,$ $|\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)|\\le 1,$ and ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, the curve $\\text{converges}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we have $\\text{a spiral}$ that is traversed $\\text{counterclockwise}.$\n\nAgain, since ${e}^{-t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ the spiral is traversed toward $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nThe $\\text{phase portrait}$ of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/05/054b319170c634494c703d9588419cb6e44414196c970ca0c39689bc62f90d97.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427138 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff6c010-8e48-535b-9136-268227d29260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426994} {:answer/id #uuid "27487e30-31ea-50af-a8c0-369003f86c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426998} {:answer/id #uuid "399a21cc-bc57-5c1a-9a89-23ec395241bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427008} {:answer/id #uuid "97963b55-7857-5df3-9428-7365708b725e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427051} {:answer/id #uuid "d366cefc-ae48-57cd-a166-9dd335e20168" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427071} {:answer/id #uuid "ef940da5-c338-5f7f-aa63-314ee88020a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27487e30-31ea-50af-a8c0-369003f86c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426998} :answer-field/id #uuid "20886724-3f12-5b6c-9a63-b9c046281dea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12bc1217-c220-572d-b0d7-d2d34eb5554c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426987} {:answer/id #uuid "35ef119c-118a-5078-8edf-efc97fc9d855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427006} {:answer/id #uuid "e30c39a5-ee5b-5079-97f3-cad9d3c0704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12bc1217-c220-572d-b0d7-d2d34eb5554c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426987} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da7c3d7-9510-5b7c-9e96-9e1ee09eb078" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "49d51940-1d42-5a6c-821f-8629f9249cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-334301" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =3\\pm 4\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=3>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010b3e6a-b894-5000-a218-c0e18a932b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426982} {:answer/id #uuid "26cdebaa-402e-5206-b419-de102d6efa8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426997} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee678fd-56a0-5e33-a7c3-4084c2657ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427012} {:answer/id #uuid "607896b3-839c-5e51-ac55-d41b15fa7f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Im}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427019} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a75b17-8edb-54a3-a586-17cb8d3b09bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427057} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc2bca0-32a3-55c2-9f6d-6acff395796b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfc2bca0-32a3-55c2-9f6d-6acff395796b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427081} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e5db6f9-3975-5145-a0d1-b564d7a77d9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "923ce9d3-b3c1-58db-8bf6-6828faae079d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a center" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427046} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0a33be-0f81-5640-8276-2f026a3ba26c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a stable spiral (sink)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427066} {:answer/id #uuid "dd70c2bc-1b35-5f8d-9da2-4e8f1c15d8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd70c2bc-1b35-5f8d-9da2-4e8f1c15d8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an unstable spiral (source)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427078} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d07975-a393-5c75-8820-6b693ddde445" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4de2f066-5f99-55ca-83ec-a830f6566d95" :question/math-academy-id "q-334303" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda =2\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$\nSince \n{{field-1}},\nthe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let $v=p+q\\text{i},$ where $p,q\\in {R}^{2},$ be an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =a+b\\text{i}.$\n\nThen, a complex solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t)=v{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nUsing Euler's formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{complex}}(t) & =v{e}^{(a+b\\text{i})t} \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt))(p+q\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+\\text{i}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\text{x}(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)+{c}_{2}{e}^{at}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q),\n$$\n\nwhere the parts $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)p-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)q)$ and $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(bt)p+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(bt)q)$ are bounded.\n\nNow, notice that $a=\\text{Re}(\\lambda )=2>0$ and ${e}^{at}={e}^{2t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty .$ Thus, we have a spiral that is traversed toward infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ \n\nTherefore, since $\\text{Re}(\\lambda )>0,$ the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable spiral (source)}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27cd716d-80c2-50e1-b8b0-30b84fb9edad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "infinity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426999} {:answer/id #uuid "80db53ca-85b4-5378-8ab0-df0ea714d433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the origin" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27cd716d-80c2-50e1-b8b0-30b84fb9edad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/re